1
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:15,748
"Seriously, you party every single day?"

2
00:00:15,748 --> 00:00:18,044
"He doesn't know, so he's not to blame."

3
00:00:18,044 --> 00:00:20,102
"I'm freezing your credit cards."

4
00:00:20,102 --> 00:00:22,281
"You must win 'The Next Leader'."

5
00:00:22,281 --> 00:00:24,383
"Din... this is Ms. Ya, our MT intern."

6
00:00:24,383 --> 00:00:25,779
"Take good care of her.

7
00:00:25,779 --> 00:00:28,992
"Do you want to enter 'The Next Leader' project?"

8
00:00:28,992 --> 00:00:30,236
"Nah..."

9
00:00:30,236 --> 00:00:32,054
"Looks pretty bougie."

10
00:00:32,054 --> 00:00:33,055
Huh?

11
00:00:33,055 --> 00:00:33,611
Huh?

12
00:00:33,611 --> 00:00:34,534
Bougie?

13
00:00:34,534 --> 00:00:35,237
Who said that?

14
00:00:35,237 --> 00:00:38,184
Talk to me, Auntie Tai!!

15
00:00:38,184 --> 00:00:45,804
[Car horn honks] / [Aunt Tai screams] / [Tires screech loudly]

16
00:00:48,203 --> 00:00:53,119
[Ambulance siren wails]

17
00:01:09,658 --> 00:01:10,229
Doctor,

18
00:01:11,616 --> 00:01:12,659
how is my aunt?

19
00:01:13,866 --> 00:01:17,316
Right now, she's in the ICU. She's in critical condition.

20
00:01:17,316 --> 00:01:19,770
Her leg injuries are quite severe.

21
00:01:19,770 --> 00:01:25,668
If the tissue dies, we'll have to consider amputating her leg.

22
00:01:27,448 --> 00:01:31,289
In any case, we'll keep evaluating her condition over the next few days.

23
00:01:31,289 --> 00:01:42,046
"I suggest getting in touch with her family soon. Long-term care and extra medication will exceed coverage."

24
00:01:42,046 --> 00:01:43,967
In any case... please make sure to contact them.

25
00:01:43,967 --> 00:01:45,602
Okay...

26
00:01:45,602 --> 00:01:47,347
Thank you...

27
00:03:37,472 --> 00:03:38,314
Hey, man!

28
00:03:39,014 --> 00:03:40,380
Don't you have any other friends?

29
00:03:41,347 --> 00:03:42,028
Sure I do

30
00:03:42,028 --> 00:03:45,895
But I'd rather be with you.

31
00:03:46,846 --> 00:03:47,477
But I don't!

32
00:03:55,595 --> 00:03:56,588
Whyyy? What's wrong with me?

33
00:03:57,595 --> 00:03:58,609
Aren't I cute?

34
00:04:14,384 --> 00:04:15,364
Are you blushing because of me? Hm?

35
00:04:21,217 --> 00:04:23,153
That's way too close...

36
00:04:23,153 --> 00:04:24,356
Do you get it?

37
00:04:24,356 --> 00:04:28,330
And another thing, I don't like anyone staring at me while I eat... Get it?

38
00:04:30,841 --> 00:04:31,341
Huh...?

39
00:04:32,465 --> 00:04:36,370
If you're not blushing, then there's no problem.

40
00:04:50,505 --> 00:04:51,171
Wait, what...?

41
00:05:29,041 --> 00:05:30,050
Should I eat like this?

42
00:05:30,050 --> 00:05:32,276
So it won't splash and stays polite,

43
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:35,504
Properly mannered and neat.

44
00:05:54,205 --> 00:05:56,289
Eating it like this... actually tastes pretty good too~

45
00:06:55,655 --> 00:06:56,603
Plumbing layouts...?

46
00:06:57,572 --> 00:06:58,405
You know how to look at those?

47
00:06:58,405 --> 00:06:59,434
Oh... it's you.

48
00:06:59,434 --> 00:07:02,410
Not really... I'm just trying to make sense of it.

49
00:07:09,695 --> 00:07:12,289
For a project like this... using Class 8.5 is more than enough.

50
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:14,393
How do you know that?

51
00:07:15,528 --> 00:07:16,295
Here... Look at this.

52
00:07:16,295 --> 00:07:20,854
The piping distance is quite long... with too many fittings... water pressure will drop.

53
00:07:20,854 --> 00:07:25,341
So if we upgrade to Class 13.5,

54
00:07:25,341 --> 00:07:29,186
it'll add about 10% to the cost, but fix the issue for good, right?

55
00:07:29,186 --> 00:07:32,768
You have to understand first that for a two- or three-story design

56
00:07:32,768 --> 00:07:34,475
Class 8.5 is enough.

57
00:07:34,475 --> 00:07:36,704
And when laying the plumbing system...

58
00:07:36,704 --> 00:07:40,195
Try to minimize using 90-degree elbows, only where necessary.

59
00:07:40,195 --> 00:07:46,141
Upgrading to 13.5 will just blow the budget... And it might not actually fix the low water pressure issue.

60
00:07:46,141 --> 00:07:52,886
You should check other areas first... Like whether they have water tanks or pumps installed... That might solve the problem more directly.

61
00:07:54,856 --> 00:07:55,776
You're pretty impressive.

62
00:07:55,776 --> 00:07:58,859
Someone like you... is exactly who I want to work with.

63
00:07:58,859 --> 00:08:02,511
By the way... Are you really not going to enter 'The Next Leader'?

64
00:08:03,855 --> 00:08:04,655
Here we go again.

65
00:08:05,729 --> 00:08:06,714
Hey... wait.

66
00:08:06,714 --> 00:08:09,165
I just think it'd be a waste of your talent...

67
00:08:09,165 --> 00:08:11,244
You understand the whole system...

68
00:08:11,244 --> 00:08:15,543
You know the costs... You get how technicians think...

69
00:08:15,543 --> 00:08:17,543
Don't you want to challenge yourself a bit?

70
00:08:19,436 --> 00:08:20,036
If I win...

71
00:08:20,036 --> 00:08:22,056
do I get a raise?

72
00:08:22,056 --> 00:08:22,556
Ya!!!

73
00:08:23,519 --> 00:08:24,700
Do I get prize money?

74
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:27,521
Absolutely. 300,000 baht.

75
00:08:30,018 --> 00:08:32,326
I get the money... so what do you get?

76
00:08:32,326 --> 00:08:34,614
I'll prove myself to...

77
00:08:35,976 --> 00:08:37,696
Ugh, don't worry about it...

78
00:08:37,696 --> 00:08:40,416
Let's just say... I want to challenge myself too.

79
00:08:40,416 --> 00:08:46,117
I just want the world to know that... Tanya can do it too.

80
00:08:50,599 --> 00:08:52,325
That sounds pretty confusing,

81
00:08:52,325 --> 00:08:53,424
I don't get it.

82
00:08:53,424 --> 00:08:55,876
You don't need to understand... Just don't look down on it.

83
00:08:57,598 --> 00:08:58,271
Deal?

84
00:09:00,431 --> 00:09:03,493
Din: Uh... Deal.

85
00:09:05,597 --> 00:09:06,597
That's what I'm talking about!

86
00:09:06,597 --> 00:09:08,101
Give it a shot...

87
00:09:21,386 --> 00:09:24,686
Today's main agenda on executive structure,

88
00:09:24,686 --> 00:09:28,479
is Mr. Itthikorn, whose term is ending this year.

89
00:09:29,969 --> 00:09:32,586
I'd like to propose bringing in next-generation management...

90
00:09:32,586 --> 00:09:34,767
for business continuity.

91
00:09:38,468 --> 00:09:40,489
I... understand what you want, sir.

92
00:09:40,489 --> 00:09:42,574
And I don't have any issue with Ya, either.

93
00:09:42,574 --> 00:09:44,331
But before we get to that...

94
00:09:44,331 --> 00:09:47,930
I'd like everyone to take a look at these numbers first.

95
00:09:50,049 --> 00:09:54,554
If we examine this... our growth this year is only 3.2%.

96
00:09:54,554 --> 00:09:57,778
Which is way off from the 7% target we set.

97
00:09:57,778 --> 00:09:59,631
The market hasn't been easy this year.

98
00:09:59,631 --> 00:10:02,813
Costs are up, and competition is fierce.

99
00:10:02,813 --> 00:10:04,482
I understand...

100
00:10:04,482 --> 00:10:15,046
But our board regulations state that executive evaluations are tied to the strategic targets approved by the board.

101
00:10:15,046 --> 00:10:17,385
And if we look at the numbers...

102
00:10:17,385 --> 00:10:21,050
There's no sign we'll reach that target.

103
00:10:21,587 --> 00:10:25,324
So Mr. Ronnayuth, you're suggesting we hold off on changing the executive structure for now, correct?

104
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:28,317
I don't mean to delay it...

105
00:10:28,317 --> 00:10:32,062
It's just that our numbers aren't looking strong right now.

106
00:10:32,062 --> 00:10:35,899
And I believe that changing things too quickly...

107
00:10:35,899 --> 00:10:39,628
Could affect market confidence in our company.

108
00:10:39,628 --> 00:10:47,112
Legally speaking... we can still extend the chairman's term if our performance targets aren't met...

109
00:10:47,112 --> 00:10:50,013
We should extend the chairman's term...

110
00:10:50,013 --> 00:10:53,595
While simultaneously recruiting for a new chairman.

111
00:10:53,595 --> 00:11:00,714
Not based on anyone's goodwill... The new chairman should be someone with proven capability and track record.

112
00:11:00,714 --> 00:11:03,041
Are you referring to The Next Leader?

113
00:11:03,041 --> 00:11:05,041
Yes, I'm going to enter a team into the competition.

114
00:11:05,041 --> 00:11:09,400
And if my team wins...

115
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:15,851
I will be the one who decides who becomes the next chairman.

116
00:11:17,038 --> 00:11:17,897
That sounds fair enough...

117
00:11:17,897 --> 00:11:19,381
Let the results speak for themselves.

118
00:11:21,079 --> 00:11:24,392
Regardless of who's a child... or who's a sibling.

119
00:11:26,829 --> 00:11:27,567
Agreed...

120
00:11:57,033 --> 00:11:57,778
Two meters.

121
00:11:57,778 --> 00:11:59,270
Perfect!

122
00:12:06,865 --> 00:12:07,865
Cutting now...

123
00:12:09,115 --> 00:12:10,181
Hey... hold on, Bro!

124
00:12:10,181 --> 00:12:10,913
What now?

125
00:12:10,913 --> 00:12:13,235
The spec sheet says two meters...

126
00:12:13,235 --> 00:12:15,140
...but that doesn't include the connector.

127
00:12:19,197 --> 00:12:20,632
So what does that mean?

128
00:12:20,632 --> 00:12:23,798
If you cut it right at two meters like this...

129
00:12:23,798 --> 00:12:26,168
once you put the fitting on, it'll be too short.

130
00:12:28,862 --> 00:12:29,406
Huh? You look completely lost.

131
00:12:29,406 --> 00:12:31,495
So how much extra length do I need to add?

132
00:12:32,778 --> 00:12:35,825
If this is a half-inch pipe,

133
00:12:35,825 --> 00:12:39,143
you need to add three centimeters for the connector.

134
00:12:39,143 --> 00:12:39,910
Three cm?

135
00:12:39,910 --> 00:12:40,733
Three cm.

136
00:12:40,733 --> 00:12:44,714
Here, add another three centimeters.

137
00:12:44,714 --> 00:12:46,386
Three cm, right? So we start from here...

138
00:12:46,386 --> 00:12:47,616
You drew a line earlier...

139
00:12:47,616 --> 00:12:48,116
Oh, right. Got it.

140
00:12:48,116 --> 00:12:49,153
Three cm.

141
00:12:49,153 --> 00:12:53,620
This one, right...

142
00:12:53,620 --> 00:12:56,327
Mm!! How's this then?

143
00:12:56,327 --> 00:12:57,839
Okay.

144
00:12:57,839 --> 00:12:59,237
Okay, right?

145
00:12:59,237 --> 00:13:00,502
Okay... that's right.

146
00:13:00,502 --> 00:13:02,244
Okay, let's do this!

147
00:13:02,244 --> 00:13:02,903
Whoa! Hold on!

148
00:13:04,774 --> 00:13:05,413
Move over here.

149
00:13:07,566 --> 00:13:08,938
Your distance is completely off.

150
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:13,746
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Hold on!

151
00:13:13,746 --> 00:13:15,517
Use the pipe cutters!

152
00:13:15,517 --> 00:13:21,807
Tsk! Oh, man!

153
00:13:21,807 --> 00:13:23,345
Oh, man...Hold the cutters...

154
00:13:23,345 --> 00:13:24,655
this way.

155
00:13:31,021 --> 00:13:32,920
Oh, man... Do you ever workout?

156
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:34,093
Huh?!

157
00:13:34,093 --> 00:13:36,611
...Sigh!

158
00:13:38,187 --> 00:13:39,743
Come on! Let's go!

159
00:13:52,726 --> 00:13:53,855
Ah! Okay.

160
00:13:54,976 --> 00:13:55,772
Okay..

161
00:13:56,893 --> 00:13:57,516
Thank you.

162
00:13:59,892 --> 00:14:00,513
Uh...

163
00:14:00,513 --> 00:14:01,296
so...

164
00:14:03,058 --> 00:14:05,409
So... should we get back to work then?

165
00:14:05,409 --> 00:14:06,495
Mm-hmm!

166
00:14:06,495 --> 00:14:07,785
I'll help you out today.

167
00:14:09,558 --> 00:14:10,079
Sure thing!

168
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,495
Uh... okay, let's do this!

169
00:14:13,495 --> 00:14:17,298
So, here's an easier way to cut the pipe, man...

170
00:14:17,298 --> 00:14:17,798
Yeah!

171
00:14:17,798 --> 00:14:18,351
You need to use the cutters.

172
00:14:18,351 --> 00:14:19,194
Mmm...

173
00:14:19,194 --> 00:14:20,565
First, you gotta hear that click sound...

174
00:14:20,565 --> 00:14:21,730
Hear the click sound first...

175
00:14:21,730 --> 00:14:23,536
Then twist it around... and press down again.

176
00:14:23,536 --> 00:14:25,271
And then it gets way easier.

177
00:14:25,271 --> 00:14:26,210
Ah, I see...

178
00:14:26,210 --> 00:14:27,288
And this distance is much safer.

179
00:14:27,288 --> 00:14:28,117
Ohhhhh, I see!

180
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:28,985
Kanghan: Got it?
Time: Mm-hmm...

181
00:14:31,138 --> 00:14:34,023
Once you're done... you just deburr the edges of the connected pipe.

182
00:14:34,023 --> 00:14:36,063
This is called a deburring tool.

183
00:14:36,063 --> 00:14:36,755
Ohooo...

184
00:14:36,755 --> 00:14:37,875
Ahem...

185
00:14:37,875 --> 00:14:40,686
That way, the fitting head will be completely smooth.

186
00:14:40,686 --> 00:14:41,213
hmm

187
00:14:42,595 --> 00:14:43,257
Do you get it or not?!

188
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:45,047
Of course I do! Keep explaining.

189
00:14:46,094 --> 00:14:47,553
Okay.

190
00:14:49,552 --> 00:14:50,226
Ain't I a great teacher?

191
00:14:50,226 --> 00:14:51,146
A little bit.

192
00:14:52,385 --> 00:14:53,008
All right...

193
00:14:53,008 --> 00:14:55,012
next step... just follow the worksheet.

194
00:14:55,012 --> 00:14:56,297
So, continuing on...

195
00:15:25,881 --> 00:15:26,517
Thank you!

196
00:15:49,295 --> 00:15:50,244
Whoa! Be careful!

197
00:15:50,244 --> 00:15:52,414
That almost stained your clothes!

198
00:15:52,414 --> 00:15:54,317
Ya: Thank you.

199
00:15:54,317 --> 00:15:58,252
Um... I'm Pong.

200
00:15:58,252 --> 00:16:00,127
I just transferred to oversee this project.

201
00:16:00,127 --> 00:16:01,278
I'm Ya.

202
00:16:03,126 --> 00:16:04,401
Oh, the Bang Na site?

203
00:16:04,401 --> 00:16:07,460
Using an 8.5 pipe gives just the right pressure.

204
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:09,713
There's no need to use a 13.5 one.

205
00:16:09,713 --> 00:16:12,883
It will also reduce costs by about 10%.

206
00:16:12,883 --> 00:16:14,677
Is the client okay with this already?

207
00:16:14,677 --> 00:16:17,173
Oh... you can read blueprints too?

208
00:16:17,173 --> 00:16:21,192
I can manage, but I'm better at planning.

209
00:16:21,192 --> 00:16:25,864
I heard you're setting up a team for The Next Leader competition?

210
00:16:25,864 --> 00:16:28,323
Word travels fast, huh?

211
00:16:28,323 --> 00:16:31,556
Well, it's a major project for the company, after all.

212
00:16:31,556 --> 00:16:33,840
It's only natural people are curious.

213
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:36,670
By the way... is your team complete yet?

214
00:16:36,670 --> 00:16:40,166
If not... may I volunteer to join and help out?

215
00:16:40,166 --> 00:16:43,547
I'm good with data analysis and field execution alike.

216
00:16:43,547 --> 00:16:46,271
Are you... actually serious about this?

217
00:16:46,271 --> 00:16:48,245
(Laughs) Ha, totally serious...

218
00:16:48,245 --> 00:16:48,745
Din: Hey!!

219
00:16:48,745 --> 00:16:49,985
Pong: Oh!

220
00:16:49,985 --> 00:16:52,750
Din: P'Chong said we have less than ten unions left in this lot.

221
00:16:52,750 --> 00:16:54,809
Din: If we don't request more, the site might stall tomorrow.

222
00:16:54,809 --> 00:16:56,864
Ya: Got it, I'll take care of it right away!

223
00:16:56,864 --> 00:16:59,847
Anyway... thank you so much.

224
00:16:59,847 --> 00:17:01,937
I'll get back to you soon.

225
00:17:01,937 --> 00:17:02,877
My pleasure.

226
00:17:04,368 --> 00:17:05,378
You're... Din, right?

227
00:17:05,378 --> 00:17:06,680
Yes!

228
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:09,205
I hope we get to work together.

229
00:17:09,205 --> 00:17:11,813
Excuse me, I'll take my leave now.

230
00:17:18,283 --> 00:17:19,821
He seems pretty interested in you...

231
00:17:19,821 --> 00:17:21,878
Why... are you jealous?

232
00:17:22,866 --> 00:17:23,829
Crazy!

233
00:17:23,829 --> 00:17:25,411
Who would even think like that?!

234
00:17:25,411 --> 00:17:26,793
I'm just kidding.

235
00:17:26,793 --> 00:17:32,266
He seems pretty capable, and he knows how to read blueprints too. If he joins your team... it'd be perfect.

236
00:17:35,739 --> 00:17:36,481
Ya: Not bad at all, right?

237
00:17:46,238 --> 00:17:46,937
What's with you standing there?

238
00:17:48,196 --> 00:17:48,941
Go back to work!

239
00:17:53,529 --> 00:17:54,071
Oooh~

240
00:17:57,195 --> 00:17:58,731
Look at you, you really are possessive!

241
00:18:08,235 --> 00:18:09,242
Oh! Let me help you with that.

242
00:18:15,859 --> 00:18:16,401
Phong: Woah!

243
00:18:16,401 --> 00:18:17,168
Housekeeper: Thank you so much.

244
00:18:17,168 --> 00:18:18,530
It's so heavy, can you handle pushing this?

245
00:18:18,530 --> 00:18:19,467
Phong: Here, let me help.

246
00:18:19,467 --> 00:18:21,157
Housekeeper: It's just a small thing, I'm fine, really.

247
00:18:22,567 --> 00:18:23,265
Housekeeper: Thank you so much.

248
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:25,794
Oh... Ms. Ya!

249
00:18:25,794 --> 00:18:27,845
Haven't you taken your lunch break yet?

250
00:18:27,845 --> 00:18:28,880
I'm just about to head out.

251
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,186
I haven't eaten yet either.

252
00:18:30,186 --> 00:18:33,296
Um... Can I join you for lunch?

253
00:18:33,296 --> 00:18:34,585
Be my guest!

254
00:18:34,585 --> 00:18:38,427
Great! That way we can keep discussing 'The Next Leader'.

255
00:18:49,730 --> 00:18:50,396
Ms. Ya.

256
00:18:50,396 --> 00:18:51,489
Here's some water for you.

257
00:18:51,489 --> 00:18:52,514
Thank you.

258
00:18:52,514 --> 00:18:55,986
Working in the shop can get pretty hot. You should drink plenty of water.

259
00:18:55,986 --> 00:18:57,542
So you don't overheat.

260
00:18:59,062 --> 00:18:59,987
Thank you, Khun Phong.

261
00:19:01,853 --> 00:19:04,006
I noticed how hard you've been working in the shop.

262
00:19:04,006 --> 00:19:05,472
You're such a hard worker.

263
00:19:05,472 --> 00:19:07,688
Oh, not really.

264
00:19:07,688 --> 00:19:10,330
I just really want to understand the work inside and out.

265
00:19:10,330 --> 00:19:12,784
So I can solve problems and improve things in the right areas.

266
00:19:12,784 --> 00:19:16,474
Wow... That's the spirit! That's how you win your staff's hearts.

267
00:19:17,768 --> 00:19:19,369
In that case, can I become your subordinate too?

268
00:19:19,369 --> 00:19:22,652
You're overpraising me, Khun Phong... I'm still just an intern.

269
00:19:22,652 --> 00:19:27,451
Just talking to you like this, I can already tell...that you have a really great mindset.

270
00:19:29,850 --> 00:19:33,306
By the way, about 'The Next Leader'... Have you found anyone yet?

271
00:19:34,266 --> 00:19:34,987
Not yet.

272
00:19:34,987 --> 00:19:37,660
If you haven't... can I join you?

273
00:19:37,660 --> 00:19:40,118
Are you serious about this?

274
00:19:40,118 --> 00:19:41,099
Of course I am.

275
00:19:41,099 --> 00:19:43,356
I can show you my work first if you like.

276
00:19:48,972 --> 00:19:49,790
Here, take a look.

277
00:19:49,790 --> 00:19:52,004
Like this one, it's a construction site just like the Bang Na one.

278
00:19:52,004 --> 00:19:56,922
We'll use 8.5-inch pipes too, and the pressure should be pretty similar.

279
00:19:56,922 --> 00:19:59,439
And this one is around Ratchaphruek...

280
00:20:11,594 --> 00:20:13,278
Aren't you going to sit with them?

281
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:15,997
Nah...

282
00:20:15,997 --> 00:20:17,260
I need to think.

283
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:19,292
I'd rather sit alone.

284
00:20:22,009 --> 00:20:22,871
Need to think?

285
00:20:28,425 --> 00:20:29,401
With that look..

286
00:20:29,401 --> 00:20:30,593
you're definitely jealous!

287
00:20:35,091 --> 00:20:36,078
Ya: You're really talented, aren't you?

288
00:20:36,078 --> 00:20:38,031
Ya: You really know your systems.

289
00:20:38,031 --> 00:20:40,730
Phong: I just have to keep improving.

290
00:21:02,129 --> 00:21:05,496
Staff 1: Hey, is Yaya really Itthikorn's daughter?

291
00:21:06,462 --> 00:21:07,323
Staff 2: Totally true!

292
00:21:07,323 --> 00:21:09,407
Staff 2: My partner works in HR... everyone's gossiping about it!

293
00:21:09,407 --> 00:21:10,993
Staff 2: everyone's gossiping about it!

294
00:21:10,993 --> 00:21:14,577
Staff 2: That Yaya didn't even want to work here in the first place.

295
00:21:14,577 --> 00:21:17,113
Staff 2: But Mr. Itthikorn forced her as punishment.

296
00:21:17,113 --> 00:21:20,253
Staff 2: He took away her car and all her credit cards!

297
00:21:20,253 --> 00:21:25,606
Staff 2: And sent Yaya here to intern instead!

298
00:21:25,606 --> 00:21:28,341
Staff 2: And if she wins 'The Next Leader'...

299
00:21:28,341 --> 00:21:30,531
Staff 2: She gets everything back!

300
00:21:30,531 --> 00:21:34,414
Staff 1: What? But it's just a dad teaching his daughter, what's wrong with that?

301
00:21:34,414 --> 00:21:36,720
Staff 2: That's the whole point!

302
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:39,831
Staff 2: The reason Yaya's being so nice to us...

303
00:21:39,831 --> 00:21:42,525
Staff 2: Is just so she can win 'The Next Leader'!

304
00:21:42,525 --> 00:21:46,311
Staff 2: And once she wins and gets everything back...

305
00:21:46,311 --> 00:21:48,330
Staff 2: You think she'd actually stick around here?

306
00:21:48,330 --> 00:21:50,201
Staff 1: Yeah... you're right.

307
00:21:50,201 --> 00:21:51,976
Staff 1: That's true...

308
00:22:03,538 --> 00:22:09,204
On-screen text: Schedule for 'The Next Leader'—Submit team list and check in tomorrow at 9:00 AM.

309
00:22:15,328 --> 00:22:16,432
Din: Go with this one. Get it sorted.

310
00:22:19,661 --> 00:22:22,204
Yaya: Oh, hey... I just ran into P' Chong earlier...

311
00:22:22,204 --> 00:22:23,653
Wait!

312
00:22:23,653 --> 00:22:25,286
What's wrong with you?

313
00:22:25,286 --> 00:22:27,691
Look at that tense face... Is something wrong?

314
00:22:29,743 --> 00:22:31,162
Can I ask you something straight?

315
00:22:31,162 --> 00:22:32,731
Yeah.

316
00:22:32,731 --> 00:22:34,795
Are you here...

317
00:22:34,795 --> 00:22:38,102
because you really want to work, or just to win 'The Next Leader'?

318
00:22:38,102 --> 00:22:39,231
What do you mean by that?

319
00:22:39,231 --> 00:22:40,698
I mean, if you win...

320
00:22:40,698 --> 00:22:44,232
You'll get your car back, your credit cards back... Everything returned, right?

321
00:22:44,232 --> 00:22:45,544
From your father, I mean.

322
00:22:45,544 --> 00:22:47,767
Who told you that?

323
00:22:47,767 --> 00:22:49,777
Does that even matter?

324
00:22:49,777 --> 00:22:54,900
Fine! My dad really did force me to intern here.

325
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:57,158
And that condition was actually real.

326
00:22:57,158 --> 00:22:58,076
But so what?!

327
00:22:58,076 --> 00:23:01,836
Is this why... you were so nice to me?

328
00:23:01,836 --> 00:23:02,336
No!

329
00:23:02,336 --> 00:23:04,071
Then what is it?

330
00:23:04,071 --> 00:23:06,336
Listen! Sure, I want to win...

331
00:23:06,336 --> 00:23:07,703
...but I never lied to anyone.

332
00:23:07,703 --> 00:23:09,862
Is this... what you call not lying?

333
00:23:09,862 --> 00:23:10,761
Then what did I lie to you about?!

334
00:23:10,761 --> 00:23:12,135
It was all for your own gain.

335
00:23:12,135 --> 00:23:14,683
Listen to me... If I was doing this for personal gain...

336
00:23:14,683 --> 00:23:16,655
I wouldn't even need to go this far.

337
00:23:16,655 --> 00:23:17,716
Then why didn't you tell me?

338
00:23:17,716 --> 00:23:19,085
Because you never asked...

339
00:23:19,085 --> 00:23:23,159
Besides, it's not like I need to go around announcing it.

340
00:23:23,159 --> 00:23:25,097
Okay!

341
00:23:25,097 --> 00:23:26,943
You're not in the wrong.

342
00:23:26,943 --> 00:23:29,110
It's my fault...

343
00:23:29,110 --> 00:23:30,560
You just didn't tell me everything

344
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:32,706
It's my own fault...

345
00:23:32,706 --> 00:23:34,215
for ending up this disappointed!

346
00:23:36,068 --> 00:23:38,413
Let's just say... I'm sorry.

347
00:23:38,413 --> 00:23:40,583
I don't think I can compete for you anymore.

348
00:23:42,025 --> 00:23:44,632
Wait! We're not done talking yet!

349
00:23:44,632 --> 00:23:47,179
I don't even know what I did wrong.

350
00:23:51,149 --> 00:23:52,729
Let's just say...

351
00:23:52,729 --> 00:23:54,668
I hope you win the competition.

352
00:23:54,668 --> 00:23:57,046
Even if I'm not on the team...

353
00:23:57,046 --> 00:23:59,017
you still have Phong.

354
00:24:00,148 --> 00:24:02,139
who's ready to support you in everything.

355
00:24:02,139 --> 00:24:04,658
But no matter how it turns out...

356
00:24:04,658 --> 00:24:06,822
or how hard you lose...

357
00:24:06,822 --> 00:24:08,313
you probably won't feel a thing.

358
00:24:08,313 --> 00:24:12,421
Because if you fall, you land on a cushion

359
00:24:12,421 --> 00:24:15,034
unlike me.

360
00:25:03,057 --> 00:25:03,826
P'Time!!

361
00:25:05,306 --> 00:25:06,419
Which way are you heading back?

362
00:25:08,639 --> 00:25:09,584
That way!

363
00:25:09,584 --> 00:25:11,712
Come on... I'll give you a ride.

364
00:25:13,014 --> 00:25:13,604
Nah, I'm good...

365
00:25:13,604 --> 00:25:14,733
It's too dusty.

366
00:25:14,733 --> 00:25:17,718
Huh? Then how do you usually get back?

367
00:25:20,138 --> 00:25:21,319
Well... I take the bus.

368
00:25:21,319 --> 00:25:23,216
The bus?

369
00:25:24,554 --> 00:25:26,744
And... how exactly does a bus have less dust?

370
00:25:31,011 --> 00:25:31,866
Here!

371
00:25:31,866 --> 00:25:34,562
It's brand new... haven't even used it yet.

372
00:25:44,635 --> 00:25:45,244
Come here...

373
00:25:45,244 --> 00:25:46,260
Huh?!

374
00:25:46,260 --> 00:25:47,107
Scoot over here!

375
00:25:47,107 --> 00:25:48,631
What are you doing?

376
00:25:48,631 --> 00:25:50,008
Putting this coat on you...

377
00:25:50,008 --> 00:25:51,086
Why put it on?

378
00:25:51,086 --> 00:25:53,283
Well, you said it's dusty, right?

379
00:25:53,283 --> 00:25:56,149
Woah, woah, woah!! What are you doing?!

380
00:25:56,149 --> 00:25:59,466
Putting this coat on you... Come on, hurry up so we can get going.

381
00:26:00,757 --> 00:26:01,965
Put your arms in!

382
00:26:12,839 --> 00:26:13,425
Let me see...

383
00:26:16,089 --> 00:26:17,188
So you don't get all dusty..

384
00:26:17,188 --> 00:26:19,288
Aren't you afraid of the dust?

385
00:26:47,918 --> 00:26:48,793
Okay!

386
00:26:48,793 --> 00:26:50,399
See? No more dust getting on you...

387
00:26:50,399 --> 00:26:52,714
Guaranteed!

388
00:26:55,125 --> 00:26:56,698
P'Time... Please let me take you home.

389
00:26:56,698 --> 00:26:58,282
Please?

390
00:27:00,625 --> 00:27:01,208
Fine!

391
00:27:01,208 --> 00:27:03,493
Let's go!

392
00:27:03,493 --> 00:27:05,238
Alright! Please hop on, sir.

393
00:27:05,238 --> 00:27:06,874
Get on the bike already!

394
00:27:06,874 --> 00:27:09,411
Look at this... Premium quality!

395
00:27:09,411 --> 00:27:10,080
Okay!

396
00:27:10,080 --> 00:27:11,931
Get on! Hurry!

397
00:27:22,122 --> 00:27:22,622
Thank you.

398
00:27:25,871 --> 00:27:26,461
Ready yet?!

399
00:27:26,461 --> 00:27:27,531
Okay, ready!

400
00:27:33,412 --> 00:27:35,035
Hold on here... It's safer.

401
00:27:35,035 --> 00:27:36,723
Right here!

402
00:28:08,699 --> 00:28:09,702
Phong: Oh! Khun Ya.

403
00:28:09,702 --> 00:28:12,360
It's so late... Why haven't you gone home yet?

404
00:28:12,360 --> 00:28:14,350
I'm just about to leave.

405
00:28:23,114 --> 00:28:26,042
Um... I heard that you had a fight with Din?

406
00:28:33,029 --> 00:28:34,202
Don't tell me...

407
00:28:34,202 --> 00:28:36,444
you haven't left because of that?

408
00:28:40,029 --> 00:28:40,668
Um... Khun Ya?

409
00:28:40,668 --> 00:28:45,170
Honestly... you don't need to care that much about Din.

410
00:28:45,170 --> 00:28:47,785
You still have me, you know...

411
00:28:50,944 --> 00:28:52,267
Just relax, okay?

412
00:28:52,267 --> 00:28:54,946
Go home and rest for tonight.

413
00:28:54,946 --> 00:29:00,150
Tomorrow at 9 AM, 'The Next Leader' contestants are registering.

414
00:29:00,150 --> 00:29:01,871
Let's meet up, okay?

415
00:29:04,400 --> 00:29:06,204
Thank you so much, Khun Phong.

416
00:29:08,358 --> 00:29:08,950
My pleasure.

417
00:29:45,478 --> 00:29:48,421
Um... is Khun Ya's team coming yet? Registration is almost closing.

418
00:29:48,421 --> 00:29:50,852
They're on their way... Please wait a moment.

419
00:29:53,394 --> 00:29:53,973
Oh! Khun Ya.

420
00:29:53,973 --> 00:29:55,382
Have you been here long?

421
00:29:55,382 --> 00:29:58,191
For a bit... This way, please.

422
00:29:59,518 --> 00:30:02,375
I'm registering on behalf of Khun Ronnayuth's team.

423
00:30:05,184 --> 00:30:06,206
What do you mean by that?

424
00:30:06,206 --> 00:30:11,653
I came to meet you just like we agreed, didn't I?

425
00:30:11,653 --> 00:30:13,391
Except that...

426
00:30:14,850 --> 00:30:17,234
I'm here representing Khun Ronnayuth's team.

427
00:30:20,182 --> 00:30:21,057
Are you tricking me?

428
00:30:21,057 --> 00:30:23,176
When did I ever trick you?

429
00:30:23,176 --> 00:30:24,712
Don't forget...

430
00:30:24,712 --> 00:30:27,326
That when I asked to join your team...

431
00:30:27,326 --> 00:30:31,156
You never actually accepted me, did you?

432
00:30:31,156 --> 00:30:34,540
Then... what are you talking about?

433
00:30:34,540 --> 00:30:38,359
Ah... or could it be...

434
00:30:38,359 --> 00:30:41,989
Was it because of last night... that gave you the wrong idea?

435
00:30:43,888 --> 00:30:44,470
If so...

436
00:30:44,470 --> 00:30:47,343
Then I'm sorry about that.

437
00:30:51,012 --> 00:30:52,775
Let me teach you a little something, Nhu Ya.

438
00:30:53,761 --> 00:30:55,542
That is... never trust anyone.

439
00:30:55,542 --> 00:30:58,947
Especially when it comes to business...

440
00:30:58,947 --> 00:31:01,707
You can't trust a single person.

441
00:31:05,301 --> 00:31:08,175
If there are no more teams, applications are officially closed.

442
00:31:22,633 --> 00:31:23,631
One week earlier.

443
00:31:57,128 --> 00:31:58,947
Hey! Why can't I see anything at all?

444
00:32:01,836 --> 00:32:02,844
Hello?!!

445
00:32:02,844 --> 00:32:04,287
Can you hear me?

446
00:32:06,627 --> 00:32:08,781
Hello?! I'm stuck in the elevator!!!

447
00:32:08,781 --> 00:32:09,989
Someone's stuck in the elevator!!

448
00:32:09,989 --> 00:32:11,965
Help! Please, help us!

449
00:32:11,965 --> 00:32:25,630
P'Time!!

450
00:32:25,630 --> 00:32:26,130
P'Time... it's okay.

451
00:32:26,130 --> 00:32:29,256
it's okay.

452
00:32:29,256 --> 00:32:34,417
it's okay.

453
00:32:34,417 --> 00:32:37,938
Take a breath, P'Time... Just breathe slowly.

454
00:32:37,938 --> 00:32:45,747
Take a breath. You're doing so great.

455
00:32:51,746 --> 00:32:54,037
You're doing so great.

456
00:32:54,037 --> 00:32:58,419
You're doing so great.

457
00:33:11,452 --> 00:33:12,785
Wait! Can we still sign up in time?

458
00:33:12,785 --> 00:33:16,906
Don't worry, sir. There's no way Din will defeat me.

459
00:33:16,906 --> 00:33:19,934
Welcome, contestants of The Next Leader.

460
00:33:19,934 --> 00:33:24,969
For your first challenge, send 1 representative per team to find 3 leaks.

461
00:33:24,969 --> 00:33:32,181
I promise, once you're done, I'll take you to a restaurant fit for Young Master Time standards.

462
00:33:32,181 --> 00:33:35,223
So I grew up adopting my dad's perfectionist ways.

463
00:33:35,223 --> 00:33:36,909
I'll be right here to take care of you.

464
00:33:36,909 --> 00:33:38,246
Are you actually wishing me well?

465
00:33:38,246 --> 00:33:42,935
If my team wins, the position of company president must be mine.
